
# 2. PRD — PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT

# FixMyCampus — Product Requirements Document

**Version:** 1.0
**Date:** 06 September 2026

---

# 1. Product Overview

FixMyCampus is a campus issue reporting and resolution platform designed to provide a structured process for reporting infrastructure problems.

The product transforms a student complaint into a traceable work item.

The basic flow is:

```text
Student Reports Issue
        ↓
Administrator Reviews
        ↓
Administrator Assigns Staff
        ↓
Staff Processes Complaint
        ↓
Staff Resolves Issue
        ↓
Student Confirms Resolution
        ↓
Complaint Closed
        ↓
Student Provides Feedback
```

---

# 2. Product Vision

The vision of FixMyCampus is to create a transparent, accountable, and easy-to-use campus complaint management system where every infrastructure issue has:

* An identifiable requester
* A responsible staff member
* A current status
* A complete timeline
* A resolution record
* A closure confirmation
* Optional feedback

---

# 3. Product Goals

The product aims to:

1. Centralize campus issue reporting.
2. Improve complaint tracking.
3. Establish staff accountability.
4. Improve communication between students and staff.
5. Reduce untracked infrastructure issues.
6. Provide administrators with operational visibility.
7. Maintain complaint history.
8. Collect feedback after resolution.
9. Provide secure role-based access.
10. Demonstrate XML-based data validation.

---

# 4. Stakeholders

| Stakeholder       | Requirement                                  |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Students          | Report and track complaints                  |
| Maintenance Staff | Process assigned complaints                  |
| Administrators    | Review and assign complaints                 |
| Institution       | Improve campus operations and accountability |

---

# 5. User Stories

### Student

As a student, I want to report an infrastructure problem so that the appropriate staff can resolve it.

As a student, I want to see the current status of my complaint so that I know its progress.

As a student, I want to communicate with assigned staff so that I can provide additional information.

As a student, I want to confirm resolution so that the complaint can be closed.

As a student, I want to submit feedback after closure.

### Staff

As staff, I want to see my assigned complaints so that I can focus on my work queue.

As staff, I want to update complaint status so that students and administrators can track progress.

As staff, I want to add remarks so that important work information is recorded.

### Admin

As an administrator, I want to view all complaints so that I can manage campus issues.

As an administrator, I want to assign complaints to staff so that responsibility is established.

---

# 6. Functional Requirements

| ID    | Requirement                                                    | Priority |
| ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
| PR-01 | Users shall authenticate through login and session management. | High     |
| PR-02 | Students shall create complaints.                              | High     |
| PR-03 | Students shall view only their own complaints.                 | Critical |
| PR-04 | Admins shall view all complaints.                              | High     |
| PR-05 | Admins shall assign complaints to staff.                       | Critical |
| PR-06 | Staff shall view only currently assigned complaints.           | Critical |
| PR-07 | Staff shall update complaint status.                           | Critical |
| PR-08 | Students shall close only their own Resolved complaints.       | Critical |
| PR-09 | Status history shall be recorded.                              | High     |
| PR-10 | Complaint-specific chat shall be supported.                    | High     |
| PR-11 | Closed complaints shall prevent new messages.                  | Critical |
| PR-12 | Notifications shall be generated.                              | Medium   |
| PR-13 | Students shall provide feedback after closure.                 | Medium   |
| PR-14 | Complaint information shall be exportable as XML.              | Medium   |
| PR-15 | XML shall support XSD and DTD validation.                      | Medium   |

---

# 7. Non-Functional Requirements

### Security

Unauthorized users must not access protected information.

### Usability

The interface must clearly separate student, staff, and admin functionality.

### Reliability

Complaint history and timestamps must be maintained consistently.

### Maintainability

Frontend, backend, database, and XML resources should remain organized.

### Compatibility

The application should operate in modern web browsers in the target local environment.

---

# 8. Success Criteria

The project is considered successful when:

* Students can register and log in.
* Students can report complaints.
* Admins can assign complaints.
* Staff can process assigned complaints.
* Staff can mark complaints Resolved.
* Students can close resolved complaints.
* Students can submit feedback.
* Notifications work.
* Chat works securely.
* Unauthorized access is blocked.
* XML export works.
* XSD validation succeeds.
* DTD validation succeeds.

---

# 9. Out of Scope

The following are outside the current product scope:

* Native Android/iOS applications.
* GPS-based technician tracking.
* Automatic technician dispatch.
* Predictive maintenance.
* External enterprise identity-provider integration.

